WEBVTT

00:16.410 --> 00:19.310
Taiyou ni me ga kurameba

00:19.310 --> 00:23.990
hikari no hate o shiru darou

00:23.990 --> 00:25.890
Hoshikuzu no nou

00:25.890 --> 00:31.730
Nante semai uchuu de boku wa ikiteru

00:31.730 --> 00:39.270
Dare ka zero kara hajimeru
koodo o sazukete kurenai ka

00:39.270 --> 00:41.840
Zoushoku sare sakuran

00:41.840 --> 00:45.870
Hako no naka shiseru koronii

00:45.870 --> 00:50.350
Kakan naki yume o ute

00:50.350 --> 00:53.520
Kodoku yo jibaku seyo

00:53.520 --> 00:57.920
Yubisaki no mirai ni

00:57.920 --> 01:01.760
donna sakurifaisu ga arou to

01:01.760 --> 01:05.430
Mune no oku de

01:05.430 --> 01:08.730
Kokoro koushin seyo

01:08.730 --> 01:12.870
Ippo kako no hibi ga

01:12.870 --> 01:15.870
toozakatte yukedomo

01:15.870 --> 01:22.940
Koishikarubeki kimi

01:41.160 --> 01:44.330
There are... two kinds of summers.

01:44.330 --> 01:45.900
So hot...

01:45.900 --> 01:48.300
Why's it... so dang...

01:48.300 --> 01:50.410
hot here?

01:50.410 --> 01:53.070
What do you... expect?

01:53.070 --> 01:56.110
I mean... it's the...

01:56.110 --> 01:59.250
summer... continent...

01:59.250 --> 02:03.250
There are... two kinds of summers...

02:03.250 --> 02:04.950
Spit it out...

02:04.950 --> 02:09.090
What're the... two kinds?

02:09.090 --> 02:12.360
I forgot... bear-o...

02:12.360 --> 02:16.020
The summer... conti... nen...

02:18.800 --> 02:20.670
- Kyrie!
- Kyrie!

02:20.670 --> 02:21.340
Hey, c'mon...

02:21.340 --> 02:23.500
Pull yourself together, bear-o!

02:24.940 --> 02:26.110
Huh?!

02:26.110 --> 02:29.280
What's this... You guys again?

02:29.280 --> 02:30.800
Agan!

02:32.010 --> 02:34.380
You're just... somehow
you're everywhere, bear-o.

02:34.380 --> 02:35.520
Well, I'm on a job.

02:35.520 --> 02:39.050
I'm just on my way to deliver some
medicine to that charity hospital up the road.

02:39.050 --> 02:41.290
Charity hospital?

02:41.290 --> 02:42.560
That's right.

02:42.560 --> 02:45.530
If you want, I'd be happy
to bring you guys along with me.

02:45.530 --> 02:49.120
That is... for a price I'd be happy to.

02:49.330 --> 02:54.200
"There are Two Kinds of Summers"

03:02.880 --> 03:05.350
Where am I?

03:09.580 --> 03:11.050
A beastman?!

03:11.050 --> 03:14.520
Relax. There's no need to be alarmed.

03:14.520 --> 03:18.420
I'm the director of this hospital.

03:21.100 --> 03:24.200
I wonder why a beastman
would establish a charity hospital...

03:24.200 --> 03:26.530
C'mon, stop being so skittish.

03:26.530 --> 03:29.700
That elephant hospital director's a
beastman all right, but he's a good guy.

03:29.700 --> 03:32.070
He's a pretty skilled doctor, too.

03:33.840 --> 03:35.380
I'm sorry to keep you all waiting.

03:35.380 --> 03:36.740
How's Kyrie?!

03:38.850 --> 03:39.940
Kyrie!

03:40.920 --> 03:42.280
Toppy!

03:42.280 --> 03:44.770
And Morte... even Agan!

03:48.120 --> 03:49.420
I'm glad you're all right, bear-o.

03:49.420 --> 03:51.790
For a moment there I
thought we might lose you, bear-o!

03:51.790 --> 03:53.530
Your friend just had a mild heatstroke.

03:53.530 --> 03:57.370
It was probably complicated by
exhaustion from the long journey.

03:57.370 --> 04:00.860
If he just recuperates for a little while,
he should be better in no ti...

04:11.810 --> 04:13.780
Morte?

04:15.620 --> 04:18.650
The basic problem here is that
Kyrie's constitution is too weak!

04:18.650 --> 04:20.590
So how about you try working
out a little and getting into shape?

04:20.590 --> 04:22.150
Eh?!

04:24.090 --> 04:26.590
Well, at least I hope
you've learned your lesson

04:26.590 --> 04:30.070
and you'll start taking the
summer continent sun more seriously.

04:30.070 --> 04:30.800
At any rate...

04:30.800 --> 04:34.470
I'm in the middle of a job
right now, so I'll be on my way.

04:34.470 --> 04:35.470
Later!

04:35.470 --> 04:38.070
That's one busy guy, bear-o...

04:38.070 --> 04:40.110
What do the two of you plan to do?

04:40.110 --> 04:46.070
Please feel free to stay here as long
as you like while your friend recuperates.

04:48.480 --> 04:52.850
Yeah well, I have to admit I was pretty nervous,
it being my first solo surgery and all...

04:53.960 --> 04:55.160
Wait for me!

04:55.160 --> 04:59.960
So I guess beastmen and humans
work side by side in this place, bear-o.

04:59.960 --> 05:03.000
I haven't been here very long myself...

05:03.000 --> 05:05.330
but I've heard that everyone
here came to this place

05:05.330 --> 05:07.940
because they share the
hospital director's philosophy.

05:07.940 --> 05:09.200
Wow, a bear!

05:09.200 --> 05:10.270
How cute!

05:10.270 --> 05:11.470
It's a bear! It's a bear!

05:11.470 --> 05:12.210
I wanna pet him!

05:12.210 --> 05:14.540
- Oh brother, bear-o!
- Me too!

05:14.540 --> 05:15.380
Here you go.

05:15.380 --> 05:18.210
This is your room... make yourselves at home.

05:18.210 --> 05:21.180
It's been so long since
I slept in a bed, bear-o!

05:25.390 --> 05:27.060
Hey, where are you from?

05:27.060 --> 05:28.620
What do you do, sir?

05:28.620 --> 05:30.890
He's not a "sir"...he's a bear!

05:30.890 --> 05:34.630
Don't call me a bear, bear-o!

05:34.630 --> 05:36.500
I'm very sorry about that.

05:36.500 --> 05:41.670
Those children all lost their parents in
the fighting between beastmen and humans.

05:41.670 --> 05:45.710
Now, by the kindness of the hospital
director, they live here in the hospital.

05:45.710 --> 05:49.180
"When it comes to the preciousness of life,
humans and beastmen are the same."

05:49.180 --> 05:52.480
"Our goal is to save as many as
we can, even if it's just a single life."

05:52.480 --> 05:55.180
That's the hospital director's philosophy.

05:55.180 --> 05:57.670
That's a very noble idea, bear-o.

05:58.590 --> 06:01.750
If he really believes it, that is.

06:14.240 --> 06:15.740
So then...

06:15.740 --> 06:18.500
Just as I thought... he's!

06:59.080 --> 07:00.880
Morte?

07:00.880 --> 07:03.750
You were moaning in
your sleep... are you all right?

07:03.750 --> 07:07.950
Y-Yeah... I guess I was having a dream.

07:10.430 --> 07:11.950
Look at that!

07:13.130 --> 07:14.900
I wonder why it's doing this.

07:14.900 --> 07:19.160
It's glowing... almost like
it's reacting to you, Kyrie.

07:20.600 --> 07:24.230
"Reacting" to me? What does it mean?

07:27.340 --> 07:30.950
I was just having a dream...

07:30.950 --> 07:34.350
Maybe the Destruct Code
is trying to show me something.

07:34.350 --> 07:36.320
Giving you dreams?

07:36.320 --> 07:38.850
It's the same dream I had before.

07:38.850 --> 07:43.160
Someone had died, and you were crying.

07:43.160 --> 07:46.360
But I wonder who it was.

07:46.360 --> 07:48.830
It's like he was asleep...

07:48.830 --> 07:51.800
A young man inside a small coffin...

07:57.170 --> 08:00.040
I apologize... I'm just
making the nightly rounds.

08:00.040 --> 08:03.810
Please try not to keep him up too late.

08:06.480 --> 08:10.880
He's really going the extra mile...
working this late for everyone's sake.

08:19.060 --> 08:21.660
There are two kinds of summers.

08:21.660 --> 08:23.230
Summers to remember...

08:23.230 --> 08:25.630
and summers to regret.

08:25.630 --> 08:27.170
Hey, you're really cute...

08:27.170 --> 08:29.540
but how come you have such a tough voice?

08:29.540 --> 08:32.170
It's none of your business, bear-o!

08:32.170 --> 08:33.510
He just said "bear-o"!

08:33.510 --> 08:34.680
That's so cute!

08:34.680 --> 08:36.040
Here, lemme pet you!

08:36.040 --> 08:37.080
- Hey! Cut it out, bear-o!
- Me too!

08:37.080 --> 08:39.480
- Me too!
- Stop petting me, bear-o!

08:39.480 --> 08:41.650
It's hot, so stop touching me
with your sweaty hands, bear-o!

08:41.650 --> 08:42.980
- Pet-pet, pet-pet...
- Pet the bear...

08:42.980 --> 08:45.510
- Cut it out, bear-o!
- Pet-pet, pet-pet...

08:46.190 --> 08:48.020
You're a popular guy, Toppy!

08:48.020 --> 08:50.730
There are two kinds of popular guys.

08:50.730 --> 08:52.490
Stop mocking me, bear-o!

08:52.490 --> 08:55.360
Hey, are you one of Toppy's friends?

08:55.360 --> 08:56.930
What do you do, sir?

08:56.930 --> 08:59.170
Oh, well, uh... I'm uh...

08:59.170 --> 09:01.340
a traveling chef?

09:01.340 --> 09:03.100
You can cook food?

09:03.100 --> 09:05.370
Awesome!

09:20.860 --> 09:21.720
So hot...

09:21.720 --> 09:26.630
You really think... they're
here on the summer continent?

09:26.630 --> 09:29.360
Yes... of course they are.

09:29.360 --> 09:33.300
My analysis is... irrefuta...

09:33.300 --> 09:34.700
Nadja!

09:34.700 --> 09:36.970
You guys alright over there?

09:43.440 --> 09:45.780
Ah! You're finally awake?

09:45.780 --> 09:49.120
What were you doin' out
there without a sunshade?!

09:49.120 --> 09:51.390
I swear, you travelers are all the same!

09:51.390 --> 09:54.460
We're from the World Salvation Committee!

09:54.460 --> 09:56.790
World Salvation Committee?

09:56.790 --> 10:02.660
Ha! Well I guess you ain't much
use to your committee there, are ya?

10:02.660 --> 10:05.670
We're grateful to you for
saving us from the heat...

10:05.670 --> 10:08.160
but you really need to watch what you say!

10:09.740 --> 10:14.000
We came here in pursuit of the
World Destruction Committee.

10:14.780 --> 10:16.980
Have you seen these three
individuals, by any chance?

10:16.980 --> 10:19.280
Ah, if it's those three you want...

10:30.530 --> 10:33.330
Vegetable sandwiches for everybody!

10:33.330 --> 10:35.630
Come an' get it!

10:43.140 --> 10:47.010
I truly must thank the three
of you for all you're doing here.

10:47.010 --> 10:51.480
They've really taken a liking to you.
Look how much fun they're having!

10:51.480 --> 10:54.780
A world where beastmen and
humans live together in harmony...

10:54.780 --> 10:56.620
Making that world a reality...

10:56.620 --> 10:59.620
That's my dream.

10:59.620 --> 11:01.860
Beautiful words.

11:01.860 --> 11:05.060
People can say anything...
as long as it's just words.

11:05.060 --> 11:07.530
Doc Elephant!

11:07.530 --> 11:10.230
Look! Look! Aren't these flowers pretty?

11:10.230 --> 11:12.300
Toppy picked 'em for me!

11:12.300 --> 11:15.140
Look at these sandwiches! Kyrie made 'em for us!

11:15.140 --> 11:17.140
C'mon doc, you eat some too!

11:17.140 --> 11:21.380
You gotta hurry, or they'll all be gone!

11:21.380 --> 11:23.640
- Hurry! Hurry!
- Easy there, easy there!

11:28.820 --> 11:32.650
Well, I'm absolutely
certain it's those three, but um...

11:32.650 --> 11:35.060
They are the World Destruction Committee.

11:35.060 --> 11:40.390
But I have to say, they sure didn't
seem like any kind of heinous criminals...

11:40.390 --> 11:41.730
Stop making excuses...

11:41.730 --> 11:44.070
and get your...!

11:44.070 --> 11:45.570
I apologize.

11:45.570 --> 11:46.830
All this heat...

11:46.830 --> 11:49.170
It seems to have made her somewhat irritable.

11:49.170 --> 11:50.840
At any rate...

11:50.840 --> 11:52.870
we have no wish to make any trouble for you.

11:52.870 --> 11:56.010
So we'd appreciate it if you could
just hand them over to us without a fuss.

11:56.010 --> 11:58.410
Now hold on there!

11:58.410 --> 12:00.680
Mr. Director!

12:00.680 --> 12:05.390
I humbly apologize for
having kept you waiting like this.

12:05.390 --> 12:07.080
You!

12:08.020 --> 12:12.630
Thank you for all your help,
Rigolet. I can take it from here.

12:12.630 --> 12:15.530
Yes, sir. I'll leave you to it, then.

12:15.530 --> 12:18.370
Both of you, please come inside.

12:18.370 --> 12:19.700
Bear-o!

12:20.540 --> 12:21.800
Kyrie!

12:21.800 --> 12:23.360
Kyrie, you alright?!

12:24.640 --> 12:25.910
You're the!

12:25.910 --> 12:28.580
Rigolet, get the ball!

12:28.580 --> 12:30.380
You're that famous warrior!

12:30.380 --> 12:33.750
The one they called the
King of Desert Slaughter!

12:33.750 --> 12:36.220
"The King of Desert Slaughter"...

12:36.220 --> 12:40.490
It's true that they once
called me by names of that sort.

12:40.490 --> 12:44.420
So... why are you running a
charity hospital, of all things?!

12:56.300 --> 13:00.340
The truth is, a certain
top-secret plan is currently underway.

13:00.340 --> 13:01.610
Top secret?

13:01.610 --> 13:03.510
Yes.

13:03.510 --> 13:07.420
That's why I can't have
you stirring up trouble right now.

13:07.420 --> 13:12.510
I'm asking you to wait just a little
while longer before we hand them over.

13:23.460 --> 13:24.930
Toppy...

13:36.010 --> 13:37.680
Kyrie, wake up!

13:37.680 --> 13:40.150
Something's wrong.

13:46.790 --> 13:48.450
Kyrie!

13:54.960 --> 13:58.230
Why would the kids be gone too?

13:59.800 --> 14:02.030
That sound!

14:02.800 --> 14:05.340
What in the world's going on?!

14:05.340 --> 14:09.310
I'll bet that elephant's
been planning this all along!

14:09.310 --> 14:10.510
But...

14:10.510 --> 14:12.480
the sound's coming from over there.

14:30.770 --> 14:33.230
Huh? Morte?

14:36.440 --> 14:39.040
I guess you caught us in the act!

14:39.040 --> 14:41.210
Caught you?!

14:41.210 --> 14:42.510
What the heck are you doing?!

14:42.510 --> 14:45.380
Tomorrow is Doc Elephant's birthday!

14:45.380 --> 14:49.450
We're secretly making a
cake so we can surprise him!

14:49.450 --> 14:51.420
Of all the foolish things!

14:51.420 --> 14:53.390
Stop horsing around with all that nonsense...

14:53.390 --> 14:55.120
and get yourselves to bed!

14:55.120 --> 14:56.420
Hey, Morte...

14:56.420 --> 14:59.450
Don't spill the beans to
the hospital director, okay?

15:06.070 --> 15:07.360
I swear!

15:17.210 --> 15:18.810
What are you...?!

15:18.810 --> 15:21.750
What's this? Your idea of a
birthday party for the hospital director?

15:21.750 --> 15:23.720
I must say, I've never seen one like this.

15:23.720 --> 15:26.950
You?! You haven't gotten away yet?!

15:26.950 --> 15:28.290
Away?

15:28.290 --> 15:32.460
A pair of World Salvation
Committee agents came by this afternoon.

15:32.460 --> 15:34.460
From the World Salvation Committee?!

15:34.460 --> 15:38.330
I made up some story to get them
to go away, but they might come back.

15:38.330 --> 15:41.170
That's why I left word that you
guys should take off as soon as...

15:41.170 --> 15:43.400
Wait... you didn't give them the message?!

15:43.400 --> 15:45.770
Why should I give them the message?

15:45.770 --> 15:49.310
We have no business covering for the
likes of the World Destruction Committee!

15:49.310 --> 15:51.980
So you... you were working for them all along?!

15:51.980 --> 15:53.080
Don't move!

15:53.080 --> 15:54.850
I won't have you getting in the way!

15:54.850 --> 15:55.850
And as for him...

15:55.850 --> 15:59.650
Before I kill him I'll make him
suffer just like my family did!

16:00.790 --> 16:02.620
What are you talking about?!

16:02.620 --> 16:07.690
I've devoted my entire life
to getting revenge on him!

16:09.130 --> 16:11.800
It's sharp now, so we can cut
the cake into nice clean slices!

16:11.800 --> 16:13.100
Yay!

16:13.100 --> 16:16.800
But Morte might be more of a
blabbermouth than we think, bear-o.

16:16.800 --> 16:20.970
All right... I'll go get her to
promise not to tell anyone!

16:21.880 --> 16:26.010
When I heard a beastman who looked just
like him was running a charity hospital here,

16:26.010 --> 16:27.780
I slipped in as a hospital worker.

16:27.780 --> 16:30.720
I had to be sure he was really the one!

16:30.720 --> 16:31.990
The one?

16:31.990 --> 16:32.890
That's right.

16:32.890 --> 16:35.320
At first I couldn't believe it, either.

16:35.320 --> 16:39.030
I never imagined there could ever
be a beastman this good in the world.

16:39.030 --> 16:42.630
I thought they must've pointed
me toward the wrong beastman.

16:42.630 --> 16:44.530
But then...

16:46.030 --> 16:50.160
I finally uncovered his true identity!

16:53.810 --> 16:59.410
I happened to overhear his conversation with
the people from the World Salvation Committee...

17:03.650 --> 17:06.810
and found out that he is
the King of Desert Slaughter!

17:08.220 --> 17:09.760
You're absolutely right.

17:09.760 --> 17:14.990
I'm the beastman who was once
known as the King of Desert Slaughter.

17:16.060 --> 17:20.100
But now I spend my life
trying to atone for my sins.

17:20.100 --> 17:21.570
Atonement?

17:21.570 --> 17:23.740
That's why you started this charity hospital?

17:23.740 --> 17:24.570
Exactly!

17:24.570 --> 17:27.240
To save as many as I can,
even if it's just a single life.

17:27.240 --> 17:31.380
You really think that's
enough to wash your sins away?!

17:31.380 --> 17:34.580
You wiped out my entire village!

17:34.580 --> 17:35.880
You killed my wife!

17:35.880 --> 17:36.950
My daughter!

17:36.950 --> 17:39.090
You did that!

17:39.090 --> 17:44.020
You're right... I have no right
to even beg your forgiveness.

17:44.020 --> 17:46.190
Do what you must.

17:52.630 --> 17:55.040
What's taking Kyrie so long, bear-o?

17:55.040 --> 17:57.070
He must've gotten caught!

17:57.070 --> 17:58.210
We've got no choice...

17:58.210 --> 18:02.540
It's a day early, but we've gotta go
ahead and bring the cake now, bear-o.

18:05.450 --> 18:06.980
What's so funny?!

18:06.980 --> 18:10.280
Are you trying to get in the way of my revenge?!

18:12.250 --> 18:16.920
Far from it! Do whatever you want to him.

18:16.920 --> 18:19.630
The same thing happened to my family.

18:19.630 --> 18:23.930
They got caught up in the fight between
beastmen and humans and got killed.

18:23.930 --> 18:28.970
My little brother joined a
resistance group called the Golden Lions.

18:28.970 --> 18:30.600
He kept saying that one day...

18:30.600 --> 18:33.470
they'd topple the beastmen
and win freedom for humanity.

18:33.470 --> 18:35.240
He was just a kid...

18:35.240 --> 18:37.910
but he bought into the
resistance hook, line and sinker!

18:37.910 --> 18:41.080
So the boy... from my dream...

18:41.080 --> 18:42.650
He was Morte's brother?

18:42.650 --> 18:46.490
This stupid existence, where the only
thing beastmen and humans can seem to do

18:46.490 --> 18:47.960
is keep on fighting forever!

18:47.960 --> 18:49.820
I wish everyone would just cease to exist!

18:49.820 --> 18:50.930
This...

18:50.930 --> 18:52.990
this stupid world can
just die off for all I care!

18:52.990 --> 18:54.830
Then let's end it right here!

18:54.830 --> 18:57.870
Let's tear it all down together!

18:57.870 --> 18:59.260
Kyrie!

19:05.640 --> 19:08.010
Happy Birthday!

19:08.010 --> 19:09.480
What's everyone...?!

19:09.480 --> 19:11.180
- Let me go!
- What's going on here, bear-o?!

19:11.180 --> 19:14.310
- Stop it!
- Hurry and get out of here!

19:19.120 --> 19:21.620
Please! Don't bring the kids into this!

19:21.620 --> 19:23.160
Everyone out of here now, bear-o!

19:23.160 --> 19:24.460
Damn you!

19:24.460 --> 19:26.190
Stay right there... or I'll light it!

19:26.190 --> 19:28.330
No, don't!

19:28.330 --> 19:29.320
Bear-o!

19:31.200 --> 19:33.000
Don't pick on our Doc Elephant!

19:33.000 --> 19:34.700
Stop picking on him!

19:34.700 --> 19:36.670
Anyone who picks on Doc Elephant...

19:36.670 --> 19:38.410
has to go through me first!

19:38.410 --> 19:40.240
Everyone...

19:45.180 --> 19:47.080
Daddy!

20:12.740 --> 20:14.170
Bear-o!

20:15.440 --> 20:17.910
Anne! Bel! Seth!

20:29.020 --> 20:30.590
But Doc Elephant's in there!

20:30.590 --> 20:32.260
I'll save him, bear-o!

20:32.260 --> 20:33.460
You can't.

20:33.460 --> 20:35.930
Not with the fire raging like that.

20:42.770 --> 20:44.870
Doc Elephant!

20:44.870 --> 20:46.370
Don't worry.

20:46.370 --> 20:50.430
A little fire like this is nothing!

20:55.080 --> 20:56.740
I'm so glad!

21:03.460 --> 21:04.890
Hey wait up, Morte!

21:04.890 --> 21:06.950
Where are you going?!

21:09.060 --> 21:12.000
You two should stay here.

21:12.000 --> 21:14.330
I'm sure you'll be safe here...

21:14.330 --> 21:17.740
and you can go back to your peaceful lives.

21:23.580 --> 21:24.810
What's your problem, bear-o?

21:24.810 --> 21:27.340
Why don't you go after her, bear-o?

21:29.020 --> 21:31.310
Go for her sake.

21:32.650 --> 21:33.790
But...

21:33.790 --> 21:38.590
It's not so you can destroy the world with her.

21:40.260 --> 21:42.960
It's because if you
continue the journey with her...

21:42.960 --> 21:47.090
maybe one day her feelings will change.

21:48.340 --> 21:52.330
After all, I was able to change.

21:55.140 --> 21:56.940
Morte...

22:00.780 --> 22:05.020
A peaceful lifestyle doesn't
suit a hero anyway, bear-o.

22:05.020 --> 22:06.490
Wait for us, Morte!

22:06.490 --> 22:07.790
Wait up, bear-o!

22:07.790 --> 22:11.130
Didn't I just tell you guys not to follow me?!

22:11.130 --> 22:12.860
Playin' the tough girl...

22:12.860 --> 22:13.960
I'm not playing tough!

22:13.960 --> 22:16.560
You are definitely playing tough, bear-o.

22:16.560 --> 22:17.530
Stop following me!

22:17.530 --> 22:20.000
- Hey, wait up!
- Admit you want us here, bear-o!

22:21.030 --> 22:24.540
Kirameku suna no umi

22:24.540 --> 22:27.670
Aoi chijou no hate

22:27.670 --> 22:33.750
Yuuyami ni ochita sora kara

22:33.750 --> 22:36.880
afuredasu kioku

22:36.880 --> 22:40.090
Gareki no you ni

22:40.090 --> 22:46.090
kasanete yuku darou

22:46.090 --> 22:49.330
Meguriau inochi

22:49.330 --> 22:52.400
Surechigau kimochi

22:52.400 --> 22:55.540
Tsumugiau kotoba

22:55.540 --> 22:58.670
Kizutsukeau mono

22:58.670 --> 23:10.780
Sore demo bokura ga aruiteku
michi wa asu e tsuzuiteru no

23:13.620 --> 23:17.460
Ima o against the world ikiru imi wa

23:17.460 --> 23:20.460
change the world hitotsu janai

23:20.460 --> 23:26.030
Namima no mukou haruka na tabi e

23:26.030 --> 23:29.600
Dakara around the world ikiru kodou

23:29.600 --> 23:33.140
To the end of the world kaze ni hibike

23:33.140 --> 23:39.110
Sono saki ni aru

23:39.110 --> 23:50.720
yakusoku no chi, tadoritsukeru made

23:53.330 --> 23:54.900
We stopped for the night at a local inn...

23:54.900 --> 23:57.830
and overheard a strange rumor!

23:57.830 --> 24:00.070
Apparently, some "World Destruction Committee"

24:00.070 --> 24:03.440
has been working all
kinds of mischief in the area!

24:03.440 --> 24:06.070
Imposters are running around calling
themselves the World Destruction Committee!

24:06.070 --> 24:08.180
I won't allow it, bear-o!

24:08.180 --> 24:10.940
Next time on World Destruction... Episode 7:

24:10.940 --> 24:13.110
"There Are Two Kinds of Companions."

24:13.110 --> 24:14.980
Morte, look over there... a hot spring!

24:14.980 --> 24:16.920
Ah, very nice! Let's take
a leisurely dip afterwards.

24:16.920 --> 24:17.780
Let's go right now!

24:17.780 --> 24:19.250
I mean, I think we should go...

24:19.250 --> 24:20.480
bear-o?
